-- title:
--   Degrees of invertible ideal sheaves add over two glued components
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field and let $x : X \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be a proper morphism with $X$ reduced. Let $c_1 : C_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ and $c_2 : C_2 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper, and for $\nu = 1,2$ let $i_\nu$ be a morphism $C_\nu \to X$ together with the identity $i_\nu$ followed by $x$ equals $c_\nu$, each $i_\nu$ a closed immersion. Assume every point of $X$ lies in the set-theoretic image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$, that the scheme $C_1 \times_X C_2$ is reduced and has finite underlying space, and fix covers $\mathcal V$, $\mathcal V_1$, $\mathcal V_2$ of $X$, $C_1$, $C_2$ by two affine opens whose union is everything and whose intersection is affine. Let $J$ be an ideal sheaf datum on $X$ which is invertible in the sense that each point of $X$ has an affine open $U$ and $f \in \Gamma(X,U)$ with the point in $X_f$ such that $J$ on the affine basic open of $f$ is generated by a single non-zero-divisor, and assume likewise that the comaps of $J$ along $i_1$ and along $i_2$ are invertible, and that the closed subscheme inclusion of $J$ followed by $x$ is finite. Then the subscheme inclusion of $J.\mathrm{comap}\,i_\nu$ followed by $c_\nu$ is finite for $\nu = 1,2$, and for every point $t$ of $\operatorname{Spec} k$ the $k$-rank of the fibre of the first composite at $t$ is the sum of the corresponding ranks for $\nu = 1,2$.
--
--   This is the additivity of the degree of an effective Cartier divisor on a proper reduced curve over an algebraically closed field which is glued transversally out of two proper closed subcurves: the degree on $X$ is the sum of the degrees of the pulled-back divisors on the two components. It is used in the computation of Euler characteristics of line bundles on the two-chart model of $X_1(p)$, towards the inertia-invariant torsion of the relevant Jacobian.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_TwoGluedCurves_isFinite_and_finrank_subscheme_comp_eq_add_of_isInvertible_comap.lean

